cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it."
type: dataset
title: "Food Trace (wss-food-trace)"
abstract: >-
  Monthly point-in-time captures of the US Food and Drug Administration's queue
  of food and colour additive petitions under review or held in abeyance. FDA
  publishes only the petitions currently open: when one is granted, denied or
  withdrawn, its row disappears from the page. Grants survive as rules in 21
  CFR, but denials and withdrawals leave no public record that the petition was
  ever filed, how long it waited, or how it ended. This dataset preserves each
  month's state of the queue as the bytes were served, with a manifest row
  recording the URL, fetch time and SHA-256 of every capture, so a petition
  that leaves the queue without a matching final rule can be identified as
  abandoned. Observations are stamped with FDA's own as-of date rather than the
  fetch time. Petitioner names are not collected.
authors:
  - name: "neldivad"
    website: "https://github.com/neldivad"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
